course: dictionary
lesson: 7720
title: Publish: making writing known to others
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To publish means to make something available for people to read or see. It can be a book, a magazine, a newspaper, or writing and pictures put online. «Charles Darwin filled notebooks on his round-the-world voyage, then worked for over 20 years before publishing his big idea in 1859.» Publishing here means sharing his idea with everyone, not keeping it in his notebooks.
explain: Use the context clues, as you would with any new word. In «Ratings are decided by trained examiners who follow published rules», the rules are known to everyone. Nobody is keeping them secret, so published means made public.
explain: You will meet publish at school too. In literacy lessons you write, edit and publish your own stories, by making a neat final copy or a class book. Before you publish anything online, think: it may stay there and be seen by many people, so never publish your address or school.
fact: Publish is a verb: publish, publishes, published, publishing.
fact: «Publish» means to print a book, magazine or newspaper and make it available for people to buy or read.
fact: «Publish» can also mean to put writing, pictures or videos online for others to see.
fact: «Publish» can mean to make information known to the public, as in «publish the results».
fact: Useful phrases: publish a book, get published, publish online, publish results.
exercise: «Charles Darwin waited over 20 years before publishing his big idea in 1859.» What does publishing mean here? | *Making the idea known to everyone | Hiding the idea in a drawer | Throwing the notebooks away | Drawing a picture of a ship
exercise: «The Wind in the Willows» was first published in 1908. What does first published mean? | Read aloud at a party for the first time | Painted on a wall in a town | Typed into a secret diary | *Printed and made available to read for the first time
exercise: Mia wants to publish her story in the class book. What is she doing? | Scribbling over her story with a pen | *Making her story available for others to read | Throwing her story away | Keeping her story secret in her bag
test: What is the best reason to think before you publish something online? | It is always deleted by the next morning | *It may stay there and be seen by many people | Only your teacher can ever see it | It will make your computer run faster
test: «When a cure works, scientists test it and publish the results.» What does publish the results mean? | Keep the results in a locked drawer | *Make the results known to the public | Test the cure again and again only | Throw the results away
exam: Which of these is safe to publish online? | Your school's name and address | *A story you wrote, with no personal details | Your phone number | Your home address
